The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (group > vdpasim->dev_attr.ngroups)
    return -EINVAL;
Reason:
The condition uses > instead of >=, allowing a group equal to ngroups to pass validation, leading to an out-of-bounds write when accessing arrays like iommu or group2asid.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
- if (group > vdpasim->dev_attr.ngroups)
-     return -EINVAL;
- if (asid >= vdpasim->dev_attr.nas)
-     return -EINVAL;
Reason:
The bounds checks are removed from vdpasim_set_group_asid because they are now performed centrally in vhost_vdpa before calling this function. This eliminates the incorrect local check and prevents the out-of-bounds access.

